# rclone

## usage

```shell
curl "https://rclone.org/install.sh" | sudo bash
# IMPORTANT(jeff): rclone v1.57 or newer is required for fstab mounting
stow -Rv rclone
```

### environment vars

- `RCLONE_CONFIG_PASS` - This is for use when we opt-in to using file encryption on our configuration file
- `RCLONE_CONFIG` - Absolute path to our `rclone` configuration file

### encryption in use

Our configuration file is encrypted. Every so often, these tokens need to be
refreshed and you will be notified of these needs by `rclone` at the time it
deems necessary. In addition, any time you wish to view or modify the existing
configuration, you will be prompted for the configuration file passphrase used
for decryption.

```shell
# This is how we encrypted our configuration file
rclone config encryption set
```

### fstab

First, ensure that you have the `rclone` mount helper binary setup.

```shell
ln -sf /usr/bin/rclone /sbin/mount.rclone
```

Then, take a look at the examples given inside `contrib/fstab` for setting up
your drive mounts.

### systemd

**See also:** `contrib/systemd/rclone.service`

### scripts

    mount.sh
    remount.sh
    umount.sh

